  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats) due on Monday 16 January 1905 (15 January was a Sunday). The members retiring by rotation were Robert Thompson, Dr James M. Moore, Edward Lunn, John McNally, J.P., and Robert Hazelton (who had retired early in 1904; his seat was not filled). Nominations were received on Thursday 5 January; \"only five members having been nominated to fill a like number of seats\", the returning officer, F. W. Pollock, declared them elected, so there was no poll. Charles William Neill, solicitor, was the only new member. Folder dated the statutory polling day. No party labels printed."
